{
  "id": "spark-kleene",
  "engine": "spark",
  "engine_version": "4.3.0",
  "title": "`AND`, `OR`, `NOT` are Kleene's; `bool_and`, `bool_or` skip NULLs",
  "verdict": "three-valued logic; boolean aggregates skip NULLs, NULL when all are",
  "area": "nulls",
  "options": [
    "three_valued_logic"
  ],
  "constructs": [
    "AND",
    "OR",
    "NOT",
    "bool_and",
    "bool_or",
    "every",
    "some",
    "any",
    "IN",
    "NOT IN"
  ],
  "settings": {
    "spark.sql.ansi.enabled": [
      true,
      false
    ]
  },
  "description": [
    "`NULL AND false` is false, `NULL OR true` true, `NOT NULL` NULL. `bool_and` and `bool_or` (`every`, `some`) skip NULLs and are NULL over NULLs only. `1 IN (2, NULL)` and `1 NOT IN (2, NULL)` are NULL."
  ],
  "reference": "`and`, `or`, `not` are Kleene's; `bool_and` and `bool_or` skip NULLs as aggregates do. Spark is native.",
  "status": "no-finding",
  "evidence": "probe",
